  1247	    truncate,
  1248	    not_null,
  1249	    default,
  1250	    strict,
  1251	):
  1252	    """
  1253	    Insert records from FILE into a table, creating the table if it
  1254	    does not already exist.
  1255	
  1256	    Example:
  1257	
  1258	        echo '{"name": "Lila"}' | sqlite-utils insert data.db chickens -
  1259	
  1260	    By default the input is expected to be a JSON object or array of objects.
  1261	
  1262	    \b
  1263	    - Use --nl for newline-delimited JSON objects
  1264	    - Use --csv or --tsv for comma-separated or tab-separated input
  1265	    - Use --lines to write each incoming line to a column called "line"
  1266	    - Use --text to write the entire input to a column called "text"
  1267	
  1268	    You can also use --convert to pass a fragment of Python code that will
  1269	    be used to convert each input.
  1270	
  1271	    Your Python code will be passed a "row" variable representing the
  1272	    imported row, and can return a modified row.
  1273	
  1274	    This example uses just the name, latitude and longitude columns from
  1275	    a CSV file, converting name to upper case and latitude and longitude
  1276	    to floating point numbers:
  1277	
  1278	    \b
  1279	        sqlite-utils insert plants.db plants plants.csv --csv --convert '
  1280	          return {
  1281	            "name": row["name"].upper(),
  1282	            "latitude": float(row["latitude"]),
  1283	            "longitude": float(row["longitude"]),
  1284	          }'
  1285	
  1286	    If you are using --lines your code will be passed a "line" variable,
  1287	    and for --text a "text" variable.
  1288	
  1289	    When using --text your function can return an iterator of rows to
  1290	    insert. This example inserts one record per word in the input:
  1291	
  1292	    \b
  1293	        echo 'A bunch of words' | sqlite-utils insert words.db words - \\
  1294	          --text --convert '({"word": w} for w in text.split())'
  1295	    """
  1296	    try:
  1297	        insert_upsert_implementation(
  1298	            path,
  1299	            table,
  1300	            file,
  1301	            pk,
  1302	            flatten,
  1303	            nl,
  1304	            csv,
  1305	            tsv,
  1306	            empty_null,
  1307	            lines,
  1308	            text,
  1309	            convert,
  1310	            imports,
  1311	            delimiter,
  1312	            quotechar,
  1313	            sniff,
  1314	            no_headers,
  1315	            encoding,
